SUMMARY:Vermont: State sales & use tax return due
DESCRIPTION:Vermont's actual rule (confirmed this session directly against 
 tax.vermont.gov\, correcting a prior secondary-sourced figure): monthly fil
 ers due the 25th of the following month\; quarterly filers due the 27th of 
 the month following the quarter (April/July/October/January)\; annual filer
 s due January 25 of the following year. These entries use the quarterly 27t
 h-day rule. | Vermont's actual rule (confirmed this session directly agains
 t tax.vermont.gov\, correcting a prior secondary-sourced figure): monthly f
 ilers due the 25th of the following month\; quarterly filers due the 27th o
 f the month following the quarter (April/July/October/January)\; annual fil
 ers due January 25 of the following year. These entries use the quarterly 2
 7th-day rule. This is a representative recurring pattern\, not a single ann
 ual deadline. | Authority: Direct fetch of tax.vermont.gov's Sales and Use 
 Tax program page this session. | Source: https://tax.vermont.gov/business/s
 ales-and-use-tax | This date is computed from a recurrence rule and may not
  reflect a later-announced change\; confirm against the cited source before
  relying on it.
